    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41306" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rēscissĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f. [rescindo, II.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a making void</i>,
				<i>annulling</i>, <i>rescinding</i>,
				<i>rescission</i> (in jurid. and eccl. Lat.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prioris decreti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					50, 9, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emptionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					43, 24, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emancipationis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					37, 4, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 57, 5</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. adv. Marc. 2,
		7</span></i>.</div>
